              "text": "- Julia has a dynamic type system: you can write code without declaring types, but the language still knows the types of values at runtime.\n- Types are used to organize data and methods: functions can work on many types, and Julia chooses the right version based on the actual argument types.\n- The type hierarchy is built around abstract and concrete types, so you can define broad categories for general behavior and specific types for efficient storage and computation."
            }
